---
title: "13 · Properties and conditions"
lesson: "Entries can carry properties. __characters/noir#gender:female__ picks only entries that have that one; $w.sfx reads a property of whatever $w rolled, so the sound matches the weather; {IF $w.kind is rain, storm: … | …} chooses by it, and a line starting with IF $w.kind is snow: is kept only when it holds."
tags: [tutorial]
---
@h3 text 16:9
style: live-action, cinematic noir
$w = __weather__
$lead = __characters/noir#gender:female__

CAST
@LEAD: $lead

SHOT 6s: tracking, slow
@LEAD walks alone down an empty street in $w, {IF $w.kind is rain, storm: the collar turned up against the water|the coat buttoned to the chin}.
IF $w.kind is snow: Her breath hangs white in the air.
SFX: $w.sfx
SFX: distant traffic
